<title>JAPAN: Japan Nov cocoa bean imports down 10.6 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Nov cocoa bean imports down 10.6 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's cocoa bean imports in November totalled 1,542 tonnes, down 10.6 percent from a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Thursday. The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Nov 96	 Oct 96	  Nov 95</p>
<p> Total		1,542	   3,481	  1,724</p>
<p>Major suppliers (in tonnes):</p>
<p> Ghana		  599	   1,802	  1,090</p>
<p> Venezuela	     25	     100	    280</p>
<p> Ecuador		350	     603	    240</p>
<p>Cumulative cocoa bean imports in the first 11 months of calendar 1996 were 47,952 tonnes, against 40,041 tonnes in the same period a year earlier. Imports of other cocoa products were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 Nov 96	 Oct 96	 Nov 95</p>
<p> Cocoa paste	  145	     173		65</p>
<p> Defatted paste     180		54		72</p>
<p> Cocoa butter     1,003	   1,775	   1,444</p>
<p> Cocoa powder     1,113	   1,060	     551</p>
<p>Chocolate</p>
<p> confectionery    2,322	   2,654	   2,128</p>
</text>
